// Long-form brand copy: the editorial pages, the Evensen story, the materials guide and
// the journal. Interface strings are written in both languages where they are rendered,
// but these are whole articles, so each locale gets its own file: `content.nb.mjs` mirrors
// this one key for key, and `content.test.mjs` fails when the two drift apart.

export const CONTENT_PAGES = {
  "/pages/our-philosophy": { title: "Circular Shoes & Our Philosophy", eyebrow: "Our philosophy", heading: "Why we exist", copy: `<p>Founded in 2017 in Oslo, Norway, by fourth-generation shoemaker Martin Evensen, New Movements has grown to become a premium leader in circular footwear. Rooted in a deep respect for nature, European craftsmanship, and family heritage, New Movements combines innovation with tradition to create refined shoes of exceptional quality.</p><p>Circularity has always been part of New Movements’ DNA — from its first shoe to launching the world’s first shoe recycling program. Today, New Movements continues its journey toward a new standard of responsible premium craftsmanship, shaping the modern wardrobe with purpose, precision, and quiet confidence.</p><h2>The problem</h2><p>Every year, the world produces around 25 billion pairs of shoes, and a staggering 95% of these end up in landfills. This not only wastes valuable materials but also contributes significantly to global pollution and resource depletion.</p><h2>Our mission</h2><p>New Movements was founded by Martin Evensen with a clear goal: to revolutionize the footwear industry by creating the perfect circular shoe. We aim to end the cycle of waste by ensuring that every pair of shoes we produce can be fully recycled, reducing environmental impact and paving the way for a more sustainable future.</p><h2>Let’s move</h2><p>To step into our shoes is to see what it’s like to buy into the circular economy. Because something happens when we begin to internalize the new movements we start, however small they are. Little drops create ripples that become waves. New Movements sets people on their own paths to nurturing and healing our planet, and inspires them to start new movements of their own.</p><h2>What we do</h2><h3>Move people</h3><p>New Movements is not just a company that makes shoes. We’re a group of people with a calling to create a business that lives in harmony with the planet – and believe in challenging others to follow suit. We are doing this through the shoes we make. This is our movement to make the world a better place.</p><h3>Design philosophy</h3><p>Our approach goes beyond aesthetics. We believe in marrying innovation with purpose, creating shoes that are not only stylish and comfortable but also designed to last and, eventually, to be recycled. This philosophy guides every decision we make, from selecting materials to designing our supply chain.</p><h3>Ethical manufacturing</h3><p>We are committed to ethical production practices. This means choosing manufacturing partners who provide fair wages, safe working conditions, and respect for their workers. Our production sites in Portugal and Spain exemplify our commitment to ethical standards, showcasing the possibility of responsible manufacturing within the fashion industry.</p><h3>Circular materials</h3><p>Every component of our shoes is chosen with the environment in mind. We prioritize organic, recycled, and recyclable materials, constantly pushing the boundaries of what’s possible to increase the sustainability of our products.</p><h2>How we do it</h2><h3>Innovation and R&amp;D</h3><p>We're at the forefront of material technology and circular design. In collaboration with leading research institutions like SINTEF, we're developing new materials and production methods that could redefine sustainability in footwear. Our projects aim to create shoes that can go from shoe-to-shoe-to-shoe in a closed-loop system.</p><h3>Recycling Program</h3><p>Our Recycling Program embodies our commitment to circularity. You can return your worn-out New Movements shoes for recycling and receive a 20% discount on your next purchase. This initiative gives materials a new life and encourages you to participate in the circular economy.</p><h3>Community and Education</h3><p>We believe in the power of community and knowledge. Through our website, social media, and NM Store events, we educate people about the importance of circular design, conscious living, and the impact of our choices. We invite you to join us in making a difference, one shoe at a time.</p>` },
  "/pages/recycle": { title: "Shoe Recycling Programme", eyebrow: "20% recycle", heading: "Why We Recycle", copy: `<p>The fashion and footwear industries contribute significantly to global waste, with over 22 billion pairs of shoes discarded annually, 90% of which end up in landfills. These shoes are largely non-recyclable, leading to massive carbon emissions and environmental degradation. At New Movements, we challenge this norm by embracing circularity as the cornerstone of a sustainable future in fashion.</p><h2>What happens to your returned shoes</h2><p>Through our NM Recycling Program, launched in 2020, we have simplified the process for you to return your worn-out shoes. Each returned pair is sent back to our manufacturers where crucial materials are carefully separated, processed, and repurposed. The extent of recyclability varies with each shoe model, reflecting our ongoing efforts to enhance material recovery and reduce waste.</p><h2>How you can return shoes</h2><p>Participating in our recycling initiative is straightforward. Simply follow the detailed instructions provided in this section to send your shoes back to us. In recognition of your contribution to sustainability, you will receive a 20% discount on your next purchase. This process not only gives your shoes a new life but also helps us collectively reduce the environmental footprint, moving closer to our goal of a fully circular value chain.</p><p>Returning your worn-out shoes helps you understand the full lifecycle of each pair. Learn more about the significant environmental impact your actions help create, and see how each shoe is transformed into a new beginning. Join us in our recycling efforts and witness the collective achievements of our groundbreaking initiatives. Together, we can redefine the future of footwear.</p><p>If you wish to recycle your worn-out New Movements shoes (and we hope you do), visit our <a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/TheZsfUEc8qxNy2j8" rel="external">NM Community Center</a> at Steen &amp; Strøm in Oslo, any of our resellers (preferably where you purchased them), or email us at <a href="mailto:store@newmovements.com">store@newmovements.com</a>.</p>` },
  "/pages/shoe-care": { title: "Shoe Care Guide", eyebrow: "Care guide", heading: "Keep your pair moving", copy: `<p>Good care keeps materials supple, protects their finish and helps your shoes perform for longer. Always remove surface dirt first, test products on a hidden area and allow shoes to dry naturally.</p><h2>Leather</h2><p>Brush away dust with a soft brush, then apply a small amount of neutral leather cream or wax with a clean cloth. Let it absorb before buffing. Avoid soaking leather and never dry it directly on a radiator or beside a heater.</p><h2>Suede and nubuck</h2><p>Use a suede brush to lift dirt and restore the nap. Treat marks gently rather than scrubbing them deeper into the material. A suitable protector spray helps repel water and stains; reapply after cleaning and always follow the product instructions.</p><h2>Technical textiles and vegan materials</h2><p>Spot-clean textile and vegan uppers with a damp cloth and mild soap. Do not use bleach, solvents or a washing machine. Once clean, let the pair air-dry at room temperature and finish with a light, material-safe protector.</p><h2>Rubber and polished surfaces</h2><p>Wipe rubberised uppers and outsoles with a damp cloth as soon as possible after contact with mud or salt. Use a dry buffing cloth on polished finishes to bring back the shine without scratching the surface.</p><h2>Everyday habits</h2><p>Loosen the laces before taking shoes off, use a shoehorn and rotate pairs so each one can rest and dry. Store them away from direct sunlight and keep the original shape with paper or a shoe tree.</p><h2>Need a little help?</h2><p>Visit our <a href="/pages/contact-us">Oslo store</a> for advice and a complimentary shoeshine. For the full story behind our materials and production, read <a href="/pages/materials">Materials &amp; production</a>.</p>` },
  "/pages/contact-us": { title: "Contact Our Oslo Shoe Store", eyebrow: "Get in touch", heading: "Contact us", copy: `<div class="contact-layout"><img src="/brand-assets/contact-store.jpg" alt="The New Movements team outside the Oslo store" width="1600" height="1067" loading="eager" decoding="async"><div class="contact-details"><p><a href="mailto:store@newmovements.com">store@newmovements.com</a></p><p><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/Pzx9rjb4sbFoEdZc7" rel="external">Get directions →</a></p><address><strong>New Movements AS</strong><br>Nedre Slottsgate 8<br>0157 Oslo, Norway</address><p>Org.: 920 443 664</p><p>For help with sizing, delivery, returns or an order, email us or visit our Oslo store.</p></div></div>` },
  "/pages/returns": { title: "Shoe Returns & Exchanges", eyebrow: "Returns", heading: "Make sure the fit is right.", copy: `<p>Free returns within 30 days and free exchanges. Try footwear indoors and keep your shoes in new condition with the original packaging until you are sure about the fit. Contact our team with your order reference for a prepaid return label and return instructions.</p><p><a href="/policies/refund-policy">Read the refund policy →</a></p>` },
  "/pages/terms-and-conditions": { title: "Terms & Conditions", eyebrow: "Terms", heading: "Terms and conditions.", copy: `<p>Your seller is New Movements AS, organisation number 920 443 664, Nedre Slottsgate 8, 0157 Oslo, Norway. Contact <a href="mailto:store@newmovements.com">store@newmovements.com</a>.</p><h2>Ordering and payment</h2><p>You must be at least 18 to order. Check the product, size, delivery destination and total before completing payment. Prices use your selected currency and include applicable taxes and duties. Delivery is free to supported destinations. Availability is checked before payment; saving checkout details does not reserve an item.</p><p>Payment is completed on the secure payment page. Keep your confirmation for support. New Movements may need additional information before accepting an order; orders for resale are not accepted.</p><h2>Delivery, returns and complaints</h2><p>The delivery service and estimate are shown in checkout. Online purchases have 30 days from delivery to request a return, with free return shipping. Items must be in new condition with packaging and labels. See our <a href="/pages/returns">returns instructions</a> and <a href="/policies/shipping-policy">delivery policy</a>.</p><p>If something is wrong with your purchase, contact us with proof of purchase and photographs. Our store policies do not limit your statutory consumer rights.</p><h2>Privacy and website use</h2><p>See our <a href="/policies/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a> for handling of order details and email subscriptions. Use the website lawfully and respect New Movements’ content and intellectual property.</p>` },
  "/pages/join": { title: "Join Our Community", eyebrow: "Join", heading: "Move with us.", copy: `<p>The New Movements community brings together footwear, art, design and the people shaping a more circular future. Follow upcoming releases and events, or visit the NM Community Center in Oslo.</p><p><a href="/pages/contact-us">Visit the flagship store →</a></p><p><a href="/pages/career-opportunities">Career opportunities →</a></p>` },
  "/pages/career-opportunities": { title: "Career Opportunities", eyebrow: "Careers", heading: "Build the next movement.", copy: `<p>New Movements is an independent Oslo brand working across footwear, material innovation, retail and community. Open roles are announced through the brand’s official channels.</p><p>For a considered open application, contact <a href="mailto:store@newmovements.com">store@newmovements.com</a> with a short introduction and relevant experience.</p>` },
  "/pages/warranty-policy": { title: "Shoe Warranty Policy", eyebrow: "Customer care", heading: "Warranty policy.", copy: `<p>If a product develops a suspected manufacturing fault, stop using it and contact New Movements with the order number, a description and clear photographs. Normal wear, accidental damage and incorrect care are assessed separately from manufacturing defects.</p><p><a href="mailto:store@newmovements.com">Contact customer care →</a></p>` },
  "/policies/privacy-policy": { title: "Privacy Policy", eyebrow: "Policy", heading: "Privacy policy.", copy: `<p>New Movements AS, Nedre Slottsgate 8, 0157 Oslo, Norway, is responsible for your customer information. Contact <a href="mailto:store@newmovements.com">store@newmovements.com</a> for privacy questions.</p><h2>Orders and customer service</h2><p>We use your name, email, phone, delivery address and order details to process payment, deliver your purchase and handle support, returns and complaints. ReAI supports our store and order management; Adyen handles payment details. Delivery information is shared with your selected carrier. Order and accounting records are retained as required by law.</p><h2>On your device</h2><p>Your bag is saved in browser storage. Your selected delivery country and currency use a preference cookie. Unfinished checkout contact and address details are saved in this browser tab for up to 24 hours, alongside server autosave, so you can return to checkout. Payment tokens and newsletter permission are not stored in that draft.</p><h2>Email</h2><p>Newsletter signup is optional. When you request the welcome offer, you receive the existing CC discount and subscribed updates. Unsubscribe using the link in any marketing email. A back-in-stock request permits one email for that item and size, expires after 180 days, and does not subscribe you to the newsletter.</p><h2>Store statistics</h2><p>Our store records page and product views, bag changes and checkout views using short-lived, random browser-tab identifiers. Analytics events exclude names, email, phone, address and URL query strings. We respect Global Privacy Control and Do Not Track. Marketing email links measure clicks; we do not use email open-tracking pixels.</p><h2>Your rights</h2><p>You can request access, correction, deletion or a portable copy of your information, withdraw permission, or object to processing by contacting us. Some records must be kept for legal obligations. You may complain to <a href="https://www.datatilsynet.no/" rel="external">Datatilsynet</a>.</p>` },
  "/policies/refund-policy": { title: "Refund Policy", eyebrow: "Policy", heading: "Refund policy.", copy: `<p>You have 30 days from delivery to request a return of an online purchase. Return shipping is free. Products must be in new condition, with their original packaging and labels.</p><p>Use the prepaid return label and return form supplied in your parcel. Pack the shoe box inside protective outer packaging; do not attach the shipping label directly to the shoe box. If the label or form is missing, contact <a href="mailto:store@newmovements.com">store@newmovements.com</a> with your order reference.</p><p>Once the return has been received and approved, allow up to 14 business days for the refund. <a href="/pages/returns">See returns and exchanges</a> for full instructions.</p>` },
  "/pages/gift-cards": { title: "Gift Card Help", eyebrow: "Customer care", heading: "Gift cards", copy: `<p>For help with an existing New Movements gift card, contact <a href="mailto:store@newmovements.com">store@newmovements.com</a> before placing your order. We will help you use your balance.</p><p>New digital gift cards are currently unavailable to buy online.</p><a class="outline-button" href="/pages/contact-us">Contact us</a>` },
  "/policies/shipping-policy": { title: "Delivery & Shipping Policy", eyebrow: "Policy", heading: "Shipping policy.", copy: `<p>Available delivery services, destination restrictions and the confirmed delivery estimate are shown in secure checkout. Taxes and duties are included for every supported destination. Delivery uses PostNord or Bring in Norway, and DHL Express to other supported destinations. PostNord delivery in Norway is free; Bring has a delivery charge. Other destinations have a shipping charge below their free-delivery threshold. Select your delivery country in the store header to see its prices and threshold. The threshold applies to goods after discounts, before shipping or gift-card payment. You will not be asked to pay import charges on delivery.</p>` },
};

export const STORY_PAGE = {
  title: "Our Shoemaking Story",
  description: "Four generations of Norwegian shoemaking, from Johnny Evensen in 1916 to New Movements today.",
  railHeading: "Fresh off the truck",
  article: (figure) => `<article class="story-copy"><h1>Our Story</h1><p>Evensen builds on a family tradition that started in 1916, when Johnny Evensen set out to create quality products that could withstand the Nordic seasons and last for generations. These values became the foundation for a family tradition of heritage craftsmanship.</p><p>Today, they form the basis of our commitment to our design philosophy and European production, with repair and recycling services. A product is only as good as the materials and people behind it.</p>${figure("/brand-assets/story-johnny.jpg", "Johnny Evensen, first generation shoemaker")}<p>That’s why our fabrics and production choices lead each decision, with price following. Our products are worn, tested, and improved in real conditions—from cities to fjords—to meet the highest standards, for you.</p><section><h2>Johnny Evensen</h2><p>Master shoemaker Nils Jonny Evensen was born in 1893 in Oslo. He served his apprenticeship under royal court shoemaker H. A. Solberg in Oslo. Further education included a pattern-making course in Germany and study stays in Leipzig and Nuremberg. He worked in Denmark until 1916. Many will still remember the shoemaker in the small house built by Peder Dahl next to Øiestad’s house on Osloveien, also known as Grytebua. The workshop, called Askim Shoe Repair Workshop, was run by Rolf Evensen and his father, and remained in operation well into the years after the war. In addition to ordinary repair work and the production of new footwear, they also stitched football boots.</p><p class="story-source">— Original text from Askim museum, Norway</p></section>${figure("/brand-assets/story-rolf.jpg", "Rolf Johnny Evensen, second generation shoemaker")}<section><h2>Rolf Johnny Evensen</h2><p>Born in 1918 in Stavern. Apprenticed under his father and qualified as a shoemaker. He served as foreman at Norrøna Skofabrikk outside Hamar until retirement. In 1936, he crafted bespoke football boots called “Even Spesial,” tailored to each individual player.</p><p>Proverbs sometimes receive confirmation in the most surprising ways. “Necessity teaches a naked woman to spin,” goes an old proverb, but Rolf Evensen could testify that necessity also teaches shoeless people to shoe themselves. During the war, people brought old handbags, suitcases, and similar items to be converted into footwear whenever possible. A suitcase on one’s feet was preferable to the paper or fish-skin shoes of the time. In 1954, Rolf Evensen left the business, while Evensen senior continued for a while longer in the old premises.</p><p class="story-source">— Original text from Askim museum, Norway</p></section>${figure("/brand-assets/story-knut.jpg", "Knut Evensen, third generation shoemaker")}<section class="story-generation story-generation--brief"><h2>Knut Evensen</h2><p>Born in 1954 in Hamar. He followed in his father’s footsteps, made moccasins, and worked in his father’s factory.</p></section>${figure("/brand-assets/story-martin.jpg", "Martin Evensen, founder of New Movements")}<section class="story-generation story-generation--brief"><h2>Martin Evensen</h2><p>Born in 1990 in Oslo. He studied retail and shoe design at the Academy of Art University in San Francisco. In 2017, Martin Evensen, fourth-generation cobbler and founder of New Movements, chose to take that legacy in a new direction: one defined by circularity, innovation, and a modern understanding of what responsible craftsmanship looks like.</p></section></article>`,
};

export const MATERIALS_PAGE = {
  title: "Shoe Materials & Care",
  description: "Care guidance for New Movements leather, suede, technical textiles and rubberised footwear.",
  careHeading: "Shoe Care",
  railHeading: "Fresh off the truck",
  guide: `<section class="materials-page"><article class="materials-guide"><h1 class="sr-only">Shoe Materials &amp; Care</h1><p>At New Movements, we create products that improve lives through comfort and conscientious design. Our commitment to quality is rooted in our heritage, inspired by Rolf Evensen, who repurposed suitcases into durable footwear during wartime shortages. Today, we honor that legacy by using premium, circular materials that are built to last and designed to be renewed.</p><p>Caring for your shoes is a vital part of closing the loop. By maintaining your materials, you extend their journey and reduce environmental impact.</p><figure><img src="/brand-assets/materials-recycled-rubber.webp" alt="Recycled rubber granules prepared for New Movements footwear" width="4032" height="3024" loading="eager" decoding="async"></figure><h2>Master Your Materials</h2><p>Every material we select requires specific attention to maintain its performance and aesthetic.</p><h3>Smooth Gold-Certified Leather</h3><p>Sourced from LWG Gold-rated tanneries, this Italian leather is thick, soft, and durable. Leather needs hydration to stay flexible. Regularly apply a high-quality leather wax to prevent drying or cracking. Finish with a protection spray to shield against water and stains.</p><h3>Suede &amp; Nubuck</h3><p>These materials offer luxury softness and breathability but are naturally porous. Use a specialized suede brush to gently remove surface dirt and restore the texture. Frequent application of protection spray is essential to maintain water resistance.</p><h3>Technical Textiles &amp; Vegan Materials</h3><p>Engineered for performance using recycled PET bottles and organic materials. These are low-maintenance and can be spot-cleaned with a damp cloth. A light coat of protection spray helps the fabric repel dirt and liquids.</p><h3>Technical Suede &amp; Nubuck</h3><p>Specialty Spanish materials engineered for everyday durability. Simply wipe with a soft, dry cloth to remove dust. Occasional protection spray enhances their inherent water resistance.</p><h3>Polished &amp; Rubberised Surfaces</h3><p>From high-shine Polido leather to weather-ready rubberised uppers. Use a soft buffing cloth for polished finishes and a damp cloth to remove mud or salt from rubberised surfaces.</p><figure><img src="/brand-assets/materials-craft.webp" alt="A New Movements craftsperson working with footwear materials" width="2715" height="4066" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure><h2>Expert Tips for the Perfect Journey</h2><p><strong>The Heat Secret:</strong> Our pure rubber outsoles may feel firm initially. Your body heat naturally softens the rubber as you walk, increasing flexibility and comfort with every step.</p><p><strong>Supportive Lacing:</strong> Always tighten your laces from the bottom up. For extra heel security, use the very top lace hole to “lock” your foot in place.</p><p><strong>Professional Maintenance:</strong> You are always welcome at our flagship store for a conversation and a <strong>free shoeshine</strong> to keep your pair in top condition.</p><h2>Closing the Loop</h2><p>New Movements is never on sale because we believe in the lasting value of our products. When your shoes finally reach the end of their life, return them to any New Movements store. We will ensure the materials are repurposed, and you will receive a <strong>20% discount</strong> on your next pair to keep the movement going.</p></article></section>`,
};

